---
import "@styles/global.module.css";
import Header from "@components/header.astro";
import Scripts from "@components/scripts.astro";
import Footer from "@components/footer.astro";
import Meta from "@components/meta.astro";
import Cursor from "@components/cursor.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <Meta name="MCFuck" description="A program to fuck with your Minecraft settings!" />
        <Scripts />
        <Cursor />
    </head>

    <body>
        <canvas id="background"></canvas>

        <!-- God damnit, I'm forced to use inline styles because Astro is stupid -->
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;">
            <Header />
            <main>
                <h1>MCFuck</h1>
        <p>MCFuck is a program that attempts to fuck with your Minecraft settings, as the name implies, without
            corrupting them.</p>
        <p>When this program finishes messing up your settings file, you'll be able to witness those changes, if your
            game starts up, in game.</p>
        <p>Since this was written purely for fun, the UI looks like so. <strong style="color: red;">Although before you
            run it and let your options file get corrupted, I highly recommend making a backup!</strong></p>
                <p>
                    <a href="https://git.lunya.pet/Lunya/MCFuck/releases">
                        <button>Download this abomination</button>
                    </a>
                </p>
            </main>
            <Footer />
        </div>

        <script is:inline defer src="/scripts/background.js"></script>
    </body>
</html>
